2:T7e8,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average kitchen renovation price in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough UK guide, a kitchen renovation may typically cost around £3,000–£8,000 for a refresh, £8,000–£18,000 for a standard replacement, or £18,000–£30,000 or more for a comprehensive renovation. Every project differs, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to fit a new kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a straightforward kitchen fitting job may typically cost around £3,000–£8,000 for labour and installation, although the amount varies with kitchen size, preparation, cabinet design, worktops, appliances and the number of trades required. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to renovate a kitchen or replace it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A renovation that keeps the existing layout and reuses sound units can be cheaper than a full replacement. However, replacing damaged cabinets or outdated services may provide better value than repeatedly repairing them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What increases the cost of a kitchen renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Common cost increases include moving plumbing or electrics, removing walls, repairing floors or plaster, choosing bespoke cabinets or premium worktops, adding an island, upgrading appliances and discovering hidden problems in an older property."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I get an accurate kitchen renovation quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Provide room measurements, photographs, a basic layout and your preferred appliances and finishes. Request an itemised quote that clearly separates labour, materials, services, building work, waste removal, VAT and exclusions."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-renovation-price","d"]
